    <section class="section">
      <div class="container two-col">
        <div class="prose">
          <h2>What we mean by car recovery</h2>
          <p>Car recovery is a broader term than breakdown recovery. Our <a href="breakdown-recovery-birmingham.html">breakdown recovery</a> page deals specifically with mechanical and electrical faults — the classic "it won't start" situation. Car recovery covers that and more: any scenario where your car needs to be collected and moved because it can't, or shouldn't, be driven. That includes mechanical faults, but also flat tyres with no usable spare, keys locked inside, cars that have picked up minor damage, and non-runners bought second-hand or at auction. It's available around the clock — see <a href="24-hour-breakdown-recovery-birmingham.html">24 hour breakdown recovery</a> for more on overnight and weekend cover.</p>
          <p>If your situation involves an actual road traffic collision rather than a mechanical problem, our dedicated <a href="accident-recovery-birmingham.html">accident recovery</a> service is built around the extra care and safety steps that a crash scene needs. Coverage spans <a href="../areas/birmingham.html">Birmingham</a> city and the surrounding West Midlands towns and villages.</p>

          <h2>Typical situations we're called out for</h2>
          <ul class="checklist">
            <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg> A flat battery that jump-starting hasn't fixed.</li>
            <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg> Keys locked inside the car with no spare set nearby.</li>
            <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg> A car that won't start at all, with no obvious cause.</li>
            <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg> Minor accident damage that leaves the car safe to load but not safe to drive.</li>
            <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg> A car bought at auction or privately that turns out not to run.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2>What to expect</h2>
          <p>When you call, we'll ask what's wrong, where the car is, and where you'd like it taken — a home address, a garage, a dealership, or storage. A recovery vehicle is sent out, the car is loaded using the appropriate method for its condition, and it's transported to your chosen destination. If the cause turns out to be something simple, like a battery that can be jump-started, we'll say so rather than automatically loading the car for the sake of it.</p>

          <div class="callout">
            <p><strong>Safety first.</strong> If your car has stopped on a fast or busy road, don't wait inside it. Move yourself and any passengers well away from moving traffic, keep hazard lights on, and call us from a safe position.</p>
          </div>

          <h2>Not sure which service you need?</h2>
          <p>If the problem is clearly mechanical — a fault that's developed while driving — our <a href="breakdown-recovery-birmingham.html">breakdown recovery</a> page covers that specifically. If your car needs to be moved for a planned reason rather than an emergency, such as relocating a non-runner, take a look at <a href="car-transport-birmingham.html">car transport</a> instead. If you're unsure, just call and describe the situation — we'll point you the right way.</p>
        </div>

