    <section class="section section--alt">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-head section-head--center">
          <span class="eyebrow">Questions</span>
          <h2>Car Recovery FAQs</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-list">
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>Do you recover cars that have been in a minor bump?<span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg></span></summary>
            <p>Yes, provided the car is safe to move using standard loading equipment. For anything more serious, or where the road is blocked or someone is injured, see our <a href="accident-recovery-birmingham.html">accident recovery</a> service, which is set up specifically for collision situations.</p>
          </details>
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>Can you recover a car with a flat tyre and no spare?<span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg></span></summary>
            <p>Yes. If there's no usable spare and the tyre can't be repaired at the roadside, we'll recover the car on a flatbed or with wheel-lift equipment so it isn't driven or dragged on a damaged tyre.</p>
          </details>
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>Do I need to be present when the car is collected?<span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg></span></summary>
            <p>In most cases, yes, or you'll need to arrange for someone else to hand over the keys and confirm the destination. Let us know when you call if you won't be at the vehicle yourself, and we'll talk through the options.</p>
          </details>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

